(global_label "V3V3_SYS" (shape passive) (at 63.5 113.03 180) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify right)) (uuid 8ae36311-3fe8-5e19-8fbd-c7001b8be8d4))
(text "J11: DET_A to GND and DET_B to SD_DET with a 10k pull-up, so the input reads low with a card inserted. The\nshield goes to GND. 100 nF + 10 uF (C64/C65) sit at the socket (DESIGN_SPEC \"Rails\": SD transients stay on the\nbuck rail); the 47 uF C66 that used to be the third one is removed - a 200 mA write burst on a rail the\nAP63203 holds with 44 uF nominal of its own COUT does not need an 0805 bulk cap at the socket as well. 10k pull-ups on\n  CMD and DAT0-DAT3 are the SD-standard idle bias and also keep DAT3/CD high for\n4-bit mode. VDD = V3V3_SYS." (at 10 152 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left top)) (uuid 051b1d4f-bb27-5527-91a7-9260e4d60d8d))
